course: dictionary
lesson: 6030
title: Melanin: the colour pigment
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Melanin is a natural dark substance found in your skin, hair and eyes. It is the reason they have their colour.
explain: Melanin also protects skin from the sun's harmful rays. «Skin also reacts to the world: it makes extra brown melanin in the sun, and burns if the sun's ultraviolet light is too strong.» So the tan you get in summer is melanin at work.
explain: More melanin makes skin darker. «Freckles are spots of extra melanin; sun makes them darker, they often fade in winter.»
explain: People with albinism have very little melanin. «An albino animal cannot make melanin, so its eyes look pink or red from the blood vessels showing through.» Without the dark colour to hide them, the blood vessels show, so the eyes look pink or red.
fact: Melanin is a noun for a natural dark pigment, the substance that gives colour to skin, hair and eyes.
fact: Melanin is uncountable, so you say «some melanin», not «a melanin».
fact: Melanin helps protect skin from the sun's harmful rays.
fact: Octopuses, squid and cuttlefish squirt ink made of melanin, and cooks use squid ink to colour pasta black.
fact: Skin also makes goosebumps when you are cold and sweats to cool you down, but melanin is what makes it darker.
exercise: «Freckles are spots of extra melanin.» What are freckles? | *Spots of extra melanin | Holes in the skin | Cold bumps on the skin | Scars from the sun
exercise: Why does melanin help your skin in the sun? | *It protects skin from the sun's harmful rays | It turns hair blue | Melanin makes the sun hotter | It stops you sweating
exercise: «People with albinism have very little melanin.» What does this mean? | They can never go outside | They have extra melanin in their eyes | They have no skin at all | *They have very little of the dark pigment that gives colour
test: «More melanin makes skin darker.» What does melanin give skin, hair and eyes? | *Colour | Heat | Weight | Sound
test: Why do cuttlefish squirt ink made of melanin? | To cool down in the sea | To make pasta black | *To hide, or to make a fake blob while they jet away | To talk to other fish
exam: «Freckles are spots of extra melanin; sun makes them darker, they often fade in winter.» Why do freckles often look darker in summer? | Winter makes melanin disappear forever | Cold water darkens them | Freckles only grow in summer | *The sun makes them darker
